{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959733-a-great-video-that-explains-the-invictus","id":959733,"title":"A great video that explains the Invictus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-29T03:18:53-07:00","id":959733,"title":"A great video that explains the Invictus","content":"I found this video online and other then it saying its for the Illuminati its a perfect intro video for the invictus. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DNt7mEfFynA?list=PL61F609A21A98AA0E\" data-code=\"DNt7mEfFynA\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DNt7mEfFynA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T06:15:36-07:00","id":959775,"title":"","content":"Well, it's more Seers of Throne introduction first and foremost. Even if practical gameplay in Secret World is more of Guardians of Veil and Mysterium. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T10:25:19-07:00","id":959892,"title":"","content":"It covers &quot;exclusive conspiracy pulling the strings in pursuit of power&quot; very well. That's just such a good tropey group concept that it's used several times in the CofD. Its not exclusive to mage or vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:05:58-07:00","id":960476,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s all about power.<br /> Grabbing it, keeping it, using it. Power is our currency. Our DNA. Our god. We control the world. We provide the blueprint and we give the instructions. We\u2019re the people in grainy photos on grassy knolls. We\u2019re the shadowy faces in smoky backrooms and darkened board rooms. We\u2019re right here, hiding in plain sight, buying and selling favors. Blackmail, treason, deceit, these are our stock and trade. We work the magic of the drunken evenings with senators and chiefs of staff. We shake down demons and negotiate with sorcerers. We have stocks in hell, and compromising photos of angels. We use any means necessary regardless of the cost because the world is a bad place, and you can either do or get done.<br /> We\u2019re the Invictus, and we\u2019re not done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:28:41-07:00","id":963910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959733-a-great-video-that-explains-the-invictus?p=959892#post959892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It covers &amp;quot;exclusive conspiracy pulling the strings in pursuit of power&amp;quot; very well. That's just such a good tropey group concept that it's used several times in the CofD. Its not exclusive to mage or vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah there are alot of groups in CoD that act like that. Changeling Freeholds, various mage groups and mage puppet groups, Mummy cults, True Fae/Huntsmen Cults, Spirit Cults, Hunter Conspiracies, the Invictus, the Godmachine, Demon Agencies, verious wealthy none supernatural groups, the groups that create Deviants.<br /> <br /> The only real splats that don't are Promeathans, Sin Eaters, Werewolves (maybe), and Beasts (although Beasts may join another organization).<br /> <br /> The CoD is a battle group of competing shadowy groups and forces, with various interests, but straight forward and strange.<br /> <br /> In fact that would be a great underlying theme to the Crossover Chronicles, the horror of being trapped between competing shadowy groups, many with alien and dangerous agendas. It can also help tie various themes together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T16:34:41-07:00","id":963967,"title":"","content":"Well, the Panopticon is basically the Illuminati by another name, so I have to agree with Wyrd that its more Seer than Invictus, simply by virtue of the symbols and names used. The giant eye in the pyramid is the classic symbol of that ministry, as are all the occult experiments and secret gatherings.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile... an Invictus house <i>can</i> look like this, but a house can also take on the form of a street gang, or a high society family and their social clique, or something vastly different, which wouldn't really be a good comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T00:18:12-07:00","id":964131,"title":"","content":"It fits the <i>ethos </i>of Invictus, but overstates their reach. I do think its ethos closer to that of Invictus than the Seers of the Throne. The Seers may relish lording it over the world, but they know that they're ultimately servants of a higher power (unless some of them sincerely hope to betray and supplant the exarchs at some point). From what I gather here, the Illuminati serves the Illuminati; the highest power to them is power itself, and they believe that they have the means and will to take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T02:39:00-07:00","id":964161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959733-a-great-video-that-explains-the-invictus?p=964131#post964131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It fits the <i>ethos </i>of Invictus, but overstates their reach. I do think its ethos closer to that of Invictus than the Seers of the Throne. The Seers may relish lording it over the world, but they know that they're ultimately servants of a higher power (unless some of them sincerely hope to betray and supplant the exarchs at some point). From what I gather here, the Illuminati serves the Illuminati; the highest power to them is power itself, and they believe that they have the means and will to take it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are the exarchs not themselves seer's of the throne. If so then that would be the seers are serving only themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:06:20-07:00","id":964225,"title":"","content":"Fits pretty well with Invictus. The gist of it being that money, people, and blood don't matter at the end of the day. Its all about the power you have to control the world around you. Ultimately, that's exactly what gets people to still flock to the Invictus in the modern era. <br /> <br /> Even more solid if you use the Prima Invicta from Danse Macabre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:47:00-07:00","id":964245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959733-a-great-video-that-explains-the-invictus?p=964225#post964225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fits pretty well with Invictus. The gist of it being that money, people, and blood don't matter at the end of the day.</div> </div> </div> </div> What. Blood doesn't matter at the end of the day? Yeah, I'm going to have to disagree so much with you on that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T06:34:29-07:00","id":964259,"title":"","content":"It matters as much as the chicken breast matters to the billionaire. Its neat, and you can attach a lot to it, but at the end of the day your power is what has blood, people, drugs, and money flowing. When you're a Tier 3 Elder Vampire as Danse Macabre talks about, and Second Edition hints at, blood is a non-issue to get. You're assumed to get the meals. The problem becomes ennui.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}